 "about": "Arm f's reading shape, one click of every kind. The parent half is research 145 §5's today (no link reaches the terminal; a click on Claude's words opens nothing; Codex's drawn address opens through the web-links reading, as does the first row of a URL Claude cut); the HEAD half is SPEC D14 and D16 applied by hand: words that are an address open the words, a cut URL opens the whole target from either row, a target under plain words opens with its hover, a refused target opens nothing and shows no hover; an opened address may be written as new URL writes it, which is what the hover shows (the mid-integration HEAD build opened the look-alike host as https://xn--pple-43d.com/). Each break turns exactly its own clause. The fix round adds the D14 inputs the grader derives a cut from (whether the words' address reaches its row's last cell, the rows after it, the rows above it) and two rows: a project file's name linked to a web page, which opens the file at both builds, and a cut-looking link whose target is not what its rows draw beside an honest cut.",
